      "text": "To solve the given problem, we need to expand the expression \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\) and then identify the coefficients \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) from the expanded form. Finally, we will calculate \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\).\n\nFirst, let's expand the expression \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\) using the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials, but extended to polynomials):\n\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) = 3x^2 \\cdot 7 + 3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) + (-5x) \\cdot 7 + (-5x) \\cdot (-2x) + 4 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot (-2x)\n\\]\n\nNow, let's perform each multiplication:\n\n\\[\n= 21x^2 - 6x^3 - 35x + 10x^2 + 28 - 8x\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine like terms:\n\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nFrom the expanded form, we can identify the coefficients:\n- \\(a = -6\\)\n- \\(b = 31\\)\n- \\(c = -43\\)\n- \\(d = 28\\)\n\nNow, we need to find the value of \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\):\n\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n\\[\n8(-6) = -48\n\\]\n\n\\[\n4(31) = 124\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2(-43) = -86\n\\]\n\n\\[\n28 = 28\n\\]\n\nNow, sum these values:\n\n\\[\n-48 + 124 - 86 + 28\n\\]\n\nFirst, add \\(-48\\) and \\(124\\):\n\n\\[\n-48 + 124 = 76\n\\]\n\nNext, add \\(-86\\) to \\(76\\):\n\n\\[\n76 - 86 = -10\n\\]\n\nFinally, add \\(28\\) to \\(-10\\):\n\n\\[\n-10 + 28 = 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{18}\n\\]",
