      "text": "To find the product \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\) and express it in the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\), we will use polynomial multiplication. Let's start by distributing each term in the first polynomial to each term in the second polynomial.\n\nFirst, distribute \\(3x^2\\) to each term in \\(7 - 2x\\):\n\\[3x^2 \\cdot 7 = 21x^2,\\]\n\\[3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) = -6x^3.\\]\n\nNext, distribute \\(-5x\\) to each term in \\(7 - 2x\\):\n\\[-5x \\cdot 7 = -35x,\\]\n\\[-5x \\cdot (-2x) = 10x^2.\\]\n\nFinally, distribute \\(4\\) to each term in \\(7 - 2x\\):\n\\[4 \\cdot 7 = 28,\\]\n\\[4 \\cdot (-2x) = -8x.\\]\n\nNow, combine all these terms:\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 21x^2 + 10x^2 - 35x - 8x + 28.\n\\]\n\nCombine the like terms:\n\\[\n-6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28 = -6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28.\n\\]\n\nSo, the polynomial can be written as:\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28.\n\\]\n\nHere, \\(a = -6\\), \\(b = 31\\), \\(c = -43\\), and \\(d = 28\\). We need to find the value of \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\):\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28.\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term:\n\\[\n8(-6) = -48,\\]\n\\[4(31) = 124,\\]\n\\[2(-43) = -86,\\]\n\\[28 = 28.\\]\n\nAdd these values together:\n\\[\n-48 + 124 - 86 + 28 = 28.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{28}.\n\\]",
