      "text": "To solve for the coefficients \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) in the polynomial \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\) resulting from the product \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\), we will expand the product step by step.\n\nFirst, distribute each term in the binomials:\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\n\\]\n\n1. Distribute \\(3x^2\\):\n\\[\n3x^2 \\cdot 7 = 21x^2\n\\]\n\\[\n3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) = -6x^3\n\\]\n\n2. Distribute \\(-5x\\):\n\\[\n-5x \\cdot 7 = -35x\n\\]\n\\[\n-5x \\cdot (-2x) = 10x^2\n\\]\n\n3. Distribute \\(4\\):\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 7 = 28\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\cdot (-2x) = -8x\n\\]\n\nNow, combine all the terms:\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 21x^2 + 10x^2 - 35x - 8x + 28\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\\[\n-6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28\n\\]\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nThus, the polynomial in the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\) is:\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nFrom this, we identify the coefficients:\n\\[\na = -6, \\quad b = 31, \\quad c = -43, \\quad d = 28\n\\]\n\nWe need to find \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\):\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term:\n\\[\n8(-6) = -48\n\\]\n\\[\n4(31) = 124\n\\]\n\\[\n2(-43) = -86\n\\]\n\\[\n28 = 28\n\\]\n\nSum these values:\n\\[\n-48 + 124 - 86 + 28\n\\]\n\nSimplify step by step:\n\\[\n-48 + 124 = 76\n\\]\n\\[\n76 - 86 = -10\n\\]\n\\[\n-10 + 28 = 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{18}\n\\]",
